# Spanish translation of TinyMUX server messages (#1419).
#
# Partial by design.  This covers the moment-to-moment player loop --
# movement, taking and dropping, giving, speech, paging, looking, the common
# refusals and the building verbs.  Untranslated msgids fall back to English,
# which is normal gettext behaviour, so the catalogue is usable at any
# coverage.
#
# NOT NATIVE-REVIEWED.  Written to be grammatical and idiomatic for a MU*
# register (informal "tu" throughout), but no native speaker has read it.
# Wording that is merely *correct* is not the same as wording a player would
# actually use, and the difference is exactly what a native speaker sees at a
# glance and a non-native one does not.  Corrections are wanted; that is the
# point of shipping it.
#
# Deliberate choices a reviewer should know about, so they can disagree with
# them on purpose rather than "fix" them by accident:
#
#   * Informal "tu", never "usted".  The English is informal and a MU* is not
#     a bank.
#   * "coger" is avoided entirely in favour of "tomar" / "recoger".  It is
#     the ordinary verb for "to take" in Spain and vulgar in much of Latin
#     America, and a game cannot ask its players which one they are.
#   * Typographic quotes are kept as the source uses them, so speech renders
#     consistently with the rest of the game rather than switching to
#     Spanish angle quotes for translated lines only.
#   * "page" is rendered "contactar", not left as an English verb.
#
# This file is distributed under the same license as the TinyMUX package.
#
# Mail tranche: the "MAIL:" prefix is deliberately NOT translated.  It is a
# subsystem tag rather than prose -- parallel to the @mail command name,
# which stays English, and to "@icmd:" which this catalogue family already
# leaves alone.  Only the sentence after it is translated.
#
#
